owers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-31T20:30:43Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T16:46:22Z","closed_at":"2026-08-11T16:46:22Z","assignee":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.2.stable, v4.6.3.stable\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1047) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900HX (32 threads) - 47.72 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn our project we always get an unknown low lever error spam from the engine:\n```\nE 0:00:01:420   instance_set_scenario: BUG, indexing did not unpair geometries from light.\n  <C++ Source>  servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp:835 @ instance_set_scenario()\nE 0:00:01:420   instance_set_base: BUG, indexing did not unpair geometries from light.\n  <C++ Source>  servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp:607 @ instance_set_base()\n```\n\nThe error does not report which objects are causing the issue; it is a low level sanity check unintelligeble by the end user.\nOver the course of a session this gets reported hundreds+ times and we have no information on what to change to fix it.\nAs of now I am unaware of any actual sideffects outside of the error log. \n \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAfter deeper investigations i was able to narrow down the repro steps to the following:\n- Have a mesh close to a light with a layer matching the cull mask of the light,\n- Now change the layer of the mesh with by using `.layers` or `.set_layer_mask()` repeatedly over some frames\n- delete the light\n- upon deletion the engine throws the low level error about the failed unpairing (without any context)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot-light-pairing-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30603107/godot-light-pairing-mrp.zip)\n\nGot an even shorter MRP:\n```\nextends Node3D\n## Minimal repro for the \"BUG, indexing did not unpair geometries from light\" engine error.\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar light = OmniLight3D.new()\n\tlight.omni_range = 10.0\n\tlight.light_cull_mask = 1 \n\tlight.position = Vector3.ZERO\n\tadd_child(light)\n\n\tvar mesh_instance = MeshInstance3D.new()\n\tmesh_instance.mesh = BoxMesh.new()\n\tmesh_instance.cast_shadow = GeometryInstance3D.SHADOW_CASTING_SETTING_ON\n\tmesh_instance.position = Vector3(0, 0, -1) # inside the light's range\n\tmesh_instance.layers = 1 # starts matching the light's cull mask so it gets paired\n\tadd_child(mesh_instance)\n\n\tprint(\"REPRO: setup done, light_cull_mask=%d mesh.layers=%d\" % [light.light_cull_mask, mesh_instance.layers])\n\tfor x in 5:\n\t\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n\tmesh_instance.layers = 2\n\tprint(\"REPRO: changed mesh layer\")\n\tfor x in 5:\n\t\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n\tprint(\"REPRO: freeing light instance now (mesh.layers=%d)\" % mesh_instance.layers)\n\tlight.queue_free()\n\tfor x in 5:\n\t\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n\tget_tree().quit()\n\n```","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_even